{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-hecke-eigenvalue","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:q-hecke-eigenvalue","kind":"proposition","title":"$q$-Hecke eigenvalues from the fibre functor","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-hecke-eigensheaf","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-fibre-functor-rigidity"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-q-hecke-eigenvalue"],"tags":["geometric-langlands","hecke-algebra","fiber-functor"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.q_hecke_eigenvalue","text":"q-hecke-eigenvalue.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:q-hecke-eigenvalue\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe with substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{M}</code> be a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Hecke eigensheaf on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Bun}_{G_q}(X)</code> (<a href=\"#def:q-hecke-eigensheaf\" data-at=\"q-geometric-langlands/q-hecke-correspondences\">q-Hecke eigensheaf</a>). Its eigenvalue <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}_q \\in \\mathrm{LocSys}_{\\check{G}_q}(X)</code> is uniquely determined by the action of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau</code> on the Hecke eigenvalue data:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{L}_q \\simeq\n  \\mathrm{Aut}^\\otimes(\\tau)\\text{-}\\mathrm{equivariantisation of }\n  \\big\\{ V_\\lambda^{(q)}(\\mathcal{L}_q)_x \\big\\}_{\\lambda, x}.</code></pre>\n<p>The rigidity of the fibre functor (<a href=\"#rem:fibre-functor-rigidity\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/qou-definition\">fibre-functor rigidity</a>) implies that this collection of Hecke eigenvalues determines <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}_q</code> up to unique isomorphism.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-hecke-eigenvalue.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"24.3.4","page":"b/prop-q-hecke-eigenvalue","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":78},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.InformationTheory.QGeometricLanglands.q_hecke_eigenvalue","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/InformationTheory/QGeometricLanglands.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
